         <h1>Frequently asked questions about cats</h1>
         <p class="intro">
           A quick guide to common cat behavior, daily care, and healthy routines. Select any question to reveal its answer.
         </p>
       </div>
     </header>

     <main id="maincontent" tabindex="-1">
       <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Cat frequently asked questions">
         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-1" id="question-1">
               Why do cats purr?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-1" aria-labelledby="question-1">
             <p>Cats often purr when they feel relaxed and secure, but they can also purr when they want comfort, are recovering from stress, or are trying to soothe themselves.</p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
               How much sleep does a cat need?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-2" aria-labelledby="question-2">
             <p>Most cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day. Kittens and senior cats may rest even longer, with short active periods spread throughout the day and night.</p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
               Why do cats knead with their paws?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-3" aria-labelledby="question-3">
             <p>Kneading usually comes from kittenhood, when nursing kittens press against their mother to stimulate milk flow. Adult cats often keep the behavior as a sign of comfort and contentment.</p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
               How often should a litter box be cleaned?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-4" aria-labelledby="question-4">
             <p>Scoop the litter box at least once a day and refresh the litter regularly. A clean box helps prevent odor and encourages consistent litter box habits.</p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
               Do indoor cats still need enrichment?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-5" aria-labelledby="question-5">
             <p>Yes. Indoor cats benefit from scratching posts, climbing spaces, toys, puzzle feeders, and short play sessions that let them chase, pounce, and explore safely.</p>
           </div>
         </div>

         <div class="example">
           <h2>
             <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-6" id="question-6">
               When should I call a veterinarian?
             </button>
           </h2>
           <div class="details" id="answer-6" aria-labelledby="question-6">
             <p>Contact a veterinarian if your cat stops eating, struggles to breathe, hides more than usual, vomits repeatedly, or shows sudden behavior changes that do not improve quickly.</p>
           </div>
         </div>
       </section>
     </main>

     <footer>
       Quiet, consistent routines usually help cats feel their best.
     </footer>
   </div>

   <script>
     const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

     function collapse(button) {
       const panel = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
       button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
       panel.hidden = true;
     }

     function expand(button) {
       const panel = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
       button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "true");
       panel.hidden = false;
     }

     function toggle(button) {
       const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
       if (isExpanded) {
         collapse(button);
       } else {
         expand(button);
       }
     }

     questions.forEach((button) => {
       collapse(button);

       button.addEventListener("click", () => {
         toggle(button);
       });

       const panel = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));
       panel.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
         if (event.key === "Escape" && button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true") {
           collapse(button);
           button.focus();
         }
       });
     });
   </script>
 </body>
 </html>

')
